---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro"
import ContactCTA from "../../components/ContactCTA.astro"
import Hero from "../../components/Hero.astro"
---
<BaseLayout title="November Events | Side Quests Colorado" description="November 2026 Events">
	<div class="stack gap-20">
		<main class="wrapper about">
			<Hero
				title="November 2026 Writing Events"
				tagline="Check out the cool events you can go to in November."
			>
				<img
					width="1553"
					height="873"
					src="/assets/november-writing.png"
					alt="An open notebook"
				/>
    </Hero>
<section>
	<h2 class="section-title">Writing</h2>
		<div class="content">
			<h3>Nov 4: Boulder Library Writers Cafe</h3>
				<p class="space-p">5:30 PM to 6:30 PM at the Main Library. </p>
				<p class="space-p">Enjoy dedicated writing time and build your writing community at Writers Cafe, a drop-in writing meet up!</p>
				<p>Check out their <a href="https://calendar.boulderlibrary.org/event/17522081" target="_blank">event calendar here</a>.</p>
		</div>
		<div class="content">
			<h3>Nov 5: Colorado Side Quests Virtual Writing Meetup</h3>
				<p class="space-p">7:30 PM to 8:30 PM via Zoom</p>
				<p><a href="https://us06web.zoom.us/meeting/register/LupsAdnfThmCqntIkQgSzw" target="_blank">Register Here</a></p>
		</div>
		<div class="content">
			<h3>Nov 5: Boulder Library Creative Writer's Critique Group</h3>
				<p class="space-p">5:30 PM to 6:30 PM at the Main Library. </p>
				<p class="space-p">This is for anyone working on a creative piece -- whether it be fiction, non-fiction, poetry, screen plays, etc. Participants will read through the pieces ahead of time, come up with helpful critiques, and discuss them at the meet up. Authors will need a copy of the critiques, whether through email or hard copy, so be prepared.   This event is not hosted by the Boulder Public Library and may be updated, changed, or canceled with little notice.  This program is produced by a community partner.</p>
				<p>Check out their <a href="https://calendar.boulderlibrary.org/event/17462186" target="_blank">View the event page</a>.</p>
		</div>
		<div class="content">
			<h3>Nov 6: Boulder Library Writers Cafe</h3>
				<p class="space-p">10 AM to 11 AM at the Main Library. </p>
				<p class="space-p">Enjoy dedicated writing time and build your writing community at Writers Cafe, a drop-in writing meet up!</p>
				<p>Check out their <a href="https://calendar.boulderlibrary.org/event/17522072" target="_blank">See more about the Writers Cafe event</a>.</p>
		</div>
		<div class="content">
			<h3>Nov 11: Edgewater Books Writing Group</h3>
				<p class="space-p">7 PM to 9 PM at Edgewater Books inside Edgewater Public Market. </p>
				<p class="space-p">The Edgewater Books writing group meets on the second Wednesday and fourth Friday of every month.</p>
				<p class="space-p">What to expect at each meeting: A few minutes of chit chat to catch up, 15 minutes to go over personal goals for the day and the day’s optional writing prompt, two 45-minute writing sprints, and 15 to 30 minutes to read aloud, ask questions, and give feedback.
No requirements to join, just an interest in writing and community!</p>
				<p>Check out their <a href="https://edgewaterbooksofcolorado.com/events/" target="_blank">Visit the Edgewater Books Website</a>.</p>
		</div>
		<div class="content">
			<h3>Nov 13: Boulder Library Writers Cafe</h3>
				<p class="space-p">10 AM to 11 AM at the Main Library. </p>
				<p class="space-p">Enjoy dedicated writing time and build your writing community at Writers Cafe, a drop-in writing meet up!</p>
				<p>Check out their <a href="https://calendar.boulderlibrary.org/event/17522073" target="_blank">See more about this Writers Cafe event</a>.</p>
		</div>
		<div class="content">
			<h3>Nov 18: Boulder Writer's Alliance</h3>
				<p class="space-p">10 AM to 1 PM at the Main Library. </p>
				<p class="space-p">This is for anyone working on a creative piece -- whether it be fiction, non-fiction, poetry, screen plays, etc. Participants will read through the pieces ahead of time, come up with helpful critiques, and discuss them at the meet up. Authors will need a copy of the critiques, whether through email or hard copy, so be prepared. This event is not hosted by the Boulder Public Library and may be updated, changed, or canceled with little notice.  This program is produced by a community partner - we hope you enjoy!</p>
				<p>Check out their <a href="https://calendar.boulderlibrary.org/event/17462480" target="_blank">See more about this Writers Cafe event</a>.</p>
		</div>
		<div class="content">
		<h3>Nov 20: Edgewater Books Writing Group</h3>
				<p class="space-p">10 AM to 12 PM at Edgewater Books inside Edgewater Public Market. </p>
				<p class="space-p">The Edgewater Books writing group meets on the second Wednesday and fourth Friday of every month.</p>
				<p class="space-p">What to expect at each meeting: A few minutes of chit chat to catch up, 15 minutes to go over personal goals for the day and the day’s optional writing prompt, two 45-minute writing sprints, and 15 to 30 minutes to read aloud, ask questions, and give feedback.
No requirements to join, just an interest in writing and community!</p>
				<p>Check out their <a href="https://edgewaterbooksofcolorado.com/events/" target="_blank">Visit the Edgewater Books Website</a>.</p>
		</div>
		<div class="content">
			<h3>DenNoWriMos November Novel Writing Events</h3>
				<p class="space-p">Daily Writing Events both in-person throughout Colorado and virtual.</p>
				<p>Check out their <a href="https://dennowrimo.org/events/" target="_blank">event calendar here</a>.</p>
		</div>
</section>
<section>
		<h2 class="section-title">Disclaimers</h2>
			<div class="content">
				<p>
				These events are not hosted by or affiliated with Colorado Side Quests in any way shape or form. Colorado Side Quests does not endorse any group or organization tied to these events. You must do your own research about any event or organization you intend to participate in. You are responsible for your own safety both in-person and online. **Use any of the content on Colorado Side Quests at your own risk.**
				</p>
			</div>
</section>
      </main>

		<ContactCTA />
	</div>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
	.space-p{
		padding-bottom: 1rem;
	}
	h3 {
		font-size: 1.25rem;
	}
	.about {
		display: flex;
		flex-direction: column;
		gap: 3.5rem;
	}

	img {
		margin-top: 1.5rem;
		border-radius: 1.5rem;
		box-shadow: var(--shadow-md);
	}

	section {
		display: flex;
		flex-direction: column;
		gap: 0.5rem;
		color: var(--gray-200);
	}

	.section-title {
		grid-column-start: 1;
		font-size: var(--text-xl);
		color: var(--gray-0);
	}

	.content {
		grid-column: 2 / 4;
	}

	.content :global(a) {
		text-decoration: 1px solid underline transparent;
		text-underline-offset: 0.25em;
		transition: text-decoration-color var(--theme-transition);
	}

	.content :global(a:hover),
	.content :global(a:focus) {
		text-decoration-color: currentColor;
	}

	@media (min-width: 50em) {
		.about {
			display: grid;
			grid-template-columns: 1fr 60% 1fr;
		}

		.about > :global(:first-child) {
			grid-column-start: 2;
		}

		section {
			display: contents;
			font-size: var(--text-lg);
		}
	}
</style>